Interpret electron microanalysis through standards, corrections, and spatial context (@mp-microprobe: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mineralogy-and-petrology, #source "../sources/NIST-Quantitative-EDS.lingua#r_7XJDCAH01NX65F6Q5YY3CBFTCF", #source "../sources/Mineralogy-and-Optical-Laboratory-Manual.lingua#r_4EH79TNHB2YMYGY79B5PV11FTG", #source "../../../../hephaestus/inquiry/metrology/applications/Chemical-and-reference-material-measurements.lingua#r_78FAVM8QZ3F7N4DQP2DDP1R7KQ", #mineralogy-and-petrology "Normalize-oxide-data-and-test-formula-assumptions.lingua#r_3S3B97TF7704BK3YVVGKTBXZ2P", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "../../../../hephaestus/materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/characterization/Bulk-trace-gas-and-spatial-chemical-analysis.lingua#r_4A8HJMDKVC1V96HWB9DCX55H79") { r_4DM5842PJRXRJHV6XXFZXGBMS1
**Read:** [Electron-excited X-ray microanalysis by EDS at 50 — Newbury and Ritchie](../sources/NIST-Quantitative-EDS.lingua#r_7XJDCAH01NX65F6Q5YY3CBFTCF), the complete paper, including methods, quantitative examples, and map discussion; [Mineralogy and Optical Mineralogy Laboratory Manual — McNamee and Gunter](../sources/Mineralogy-and-Optical-Laboratory-Manual.lingua#r_4EH79TNHB2YMYGY79B5PV11FTG), the full XRD/SEM and equipment context; [Chemical measurements — matrix, recovery, selectivity, and reference material](../../../../hephaestus/inquiry/metrology/applications/Chemical-and-reference-material-measurements.lingua#r_78FAVM8QZ3F7N4DQP2DDP1R7KQ), the shared calibration/reference-material account.

Electron-excited X-ray analysis relates detected characteristic signals to composition through specimen/instrument geometry, standards, background/interference treatment, and physical corrections. EDS and WDS have different implementations and tradeoffs; performance claims need actual conditions, calibration, and uncertainty.

The beam position is not the whole interaction volume. Fine lamellae, inclusions, grain boundaries, surface coatings, roughness, damage, and adjacent phases can affect the analysis. Backscattered-electron contrast and an elemental map help target domains but require their own observation model before being translated into composition.

Analytical totals, unmeasured light/volatile components, oxidation-state assumptions, normalization, and detection limits affect a mineral formula. A plausible total does not prove a single-phase analysis, while a low total is a diagnostic question rather than permission to rescale until the expected formula appears.

**Work:** read the complete NIST paper and reconstruct a quantitative example from standards through corrected composition and uncertainty. Compare a standard-based and a clearly specified alternative approach, preserving specimen/matrix and interference conditions. Design a domain-aware analysis of a zoned or intergrown grain and identify an independent check for mixing, alteration, or beam-induced change.

Use actual instrument supervision and suitable known materials for practical work. Literature/supplied-data reproduction demonstrates analytical reasoning within its scope; it does not demonstrate operating or calibrating an instrument merely because the code or table can be reopened.

**Continue:** [Derive a mineral formula from oxide data without hiding its assumptions](Normalize-oxide-data-and-test-formula-assumptions.lingua#r_3S3B97TF7704BK3YVVGKTBXZ2P).

